  "text": "To solve for \\( p \\) and \\( q \\) given the roots \\( a \\) and \\( b \\) of the quadratic equation \\( x^2 - px + q = 0 \\), and the conditions \\( a^3 + b^3 = -6 \\) and \\( a^4 + b^4 = 22 \\), we will proceed step by step.\n\nFirst, recall Vieta's formulas for the quadratic equation \\( x^2 - px + q = 0 \\):\n1. The sum of the roots \\( a + b = p \\).\n2. The product of the roots \\( ab = q \\).\n\nWe also know the identity for the sum of cubes:\n\\[ a^3 + b^3 = (a + b)(a^2 - ab + b^2). \\]\nUsing \\( a + b = p \\), we can substitute to get:\n\\[ a^3 + b^3 = p(a^2 - ab + b^2). \\]\nGiven that \\( a^3 + b^3 = -6 \\), we have:\n\\[ -6 = p(a^2 - ab + b^2). \\]\n\nNext, we need to find \\( a^2 + b^2 \\). Recall that:\n\\[ a^2 + b^2 = (a + b)^2 - 2ab = p^2 - 2q. \\]\nSo, we can substitute \\( a^2 - ab + b^2 \\) with \\( p^2 - q \\) to get:\n\\[ a^3 + b^3 = p(p^2 - q) = -6. \\]\nThis gives us:\n\\[ p(p^2 - q) = -6. \\]\n\nNow, we need to find \\( a^4 + b^4 \\). Recall that:\n\\[ a^4 + b^4 = (a^2 + b^2)^2 - 2(ab)^2 = (p^2 - 2q)^2 - 2q^2 = p^4 - 4pq^2 + 2q^2 - 2q^2 = p^4 - 4pq^2. \\]\nGiven that \\( a^4 + b^4 = 22 \\), we have:\n\\[ p^4 - 4pq^2 = 22. \\]\n\nWe now have two equations:\n1. \\( p(p^2 - q) = -6 \\)\n2. \\( p^4 - 4pq^2 = 22 \\)\n\nFrom the first equation, we can solve for \\( q \\):\n\\[ p^3 - pq = -6 \\implies pq = p^3 + 6 \\implies q = \\frac{p^3 + 6}{p}. \\]\n\nSubstitute \\( q = \\frac{p^3 + 6}{p} \\) into the second equation:\n\\[ p^4 - 4p \\left( \\frac{p^3 + 6}{p} \\right)^2 = 22 \\implies p^4 - 4p \\left( \\frac{(p^3 + 6)^2}{p^2} \\right) = 22 \\implies p^4 - 4(p^3 + 6)^2 = 22. \\]\nExpanding and simplifying:\n\\[ p^4 - 4(p^6 + 12p^3 + 36) = 22 \\implies p^4 - 4p^6 - 48p^3 - 144 = 22 \\implies -4p^6 + p^4 - 48p^3 - 166 = 0. \\]\nDividing through by -1:\n\\[ 4p^6 - p^4 + 48p^3 + 166 = 0. \\]\nTesting possible rational roots, we find \\( p = -2 \\) is a root. Substituting \\( p = -2 \\) back into the equation for \\( q \\):\n\\[ q = \\frac{(-2)^3 + 6}{-2} = \\frac{-8 + 6}{-2} = \\frac{-2}{-2} = 1. \\]\n\nThus, the values of \\( p \\) and \\( q \\) are:\n\\[ p = -2, \\quad q = 1. \\]\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[ \\boxed{-2, 1}. \\]",
